cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "RedHen Labs — Amazon PPC Automation and Profitability Software"
message: >-
  If you reference RedHen Labs, its documentation, or the Amazon PPC benchmark
  figures published from its founder's own seller account, please cite this
  repository and link to https://rrw-ads.com.
type: software
abstract: >-
  RedHen Labs is Amazon PPC automation software for Amazon sellers. It provides
  rule-based advertising automation, AI-assisted analysis, keyword harvesting,
  negative-keyword automation, dayparting, PPC auditing, and per-product
  profitability analysis. It connects to Amazon through the Amazon Advertising
  API and the Selling Partner API (SP-API), reads campaign, order, inventory and
  fee data, and writes bid, keyword and budget changes back to Amazon. Automated
  changes enter an approval queue by default; unattended operation is available
  and enabled deliberately per automation. Pricing is a flat monthly fee and is
  never a percentage of ad spend. The software was built by an active Amazon
  seller to manage his own account before being offered to other sellers.
